# 65 — Functional documentation

## Purpose
Keep the written description of each feature aligned with what the code does after a change.

## When it applies
Every change in `passion-api` that changes what a person or another system can do: an endpoint,
workflow, permission, status, money rule, schema the product relies on, or side effect. It also
applies when the same change is made in `../passion`.

Skip formatting, comments, local renames, and test-only edits that do not change that behavior.

## Where the doc lives
One description per feature. Do not copy it into both repos.

| The change is about | Update this file |
|---|---|
| Doorloom, the online calendar, or stay sync with Doorloom | `docs/DOORLOOM.md` |
| GRN, goods receipt, or frozen GRN cost | `docs/GRN_MODULE.md` |
| Store requisition, Main Store, or the POS stock path in the ERP SOP | `docs/PASSION_ERP_WORKFLOW_SOP.md` |
| QZ Tray install or signing | `../passion/QZ_TRAY_SETUP.md` |
| A fact stated in `PASSION_LARAVEL_ARCHITECTURE.md` (route, permission, status, owner class, JSON key, event name) | That section only |
| A fact stated in `../passion/PASSION_FRONTEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` | That section only |
| Any other workflow that has no doc yet | Create `docs/<TOPIC>.md` |

Search `docs/` before creating a file. Extend the existing doc when the feature is already described.

## Required behavior
- Before finishing, read the matching doc and rewrite every sentence the change made false.
- A new doc uses the same voice as `docs/DOORLOOM.md`: what the product does now, the screen and the endpoint, permission names, status strings, and a short "not included" note. No recommendations.
- A feature that spans the API and the Next.js screen is one file under `docs/`. Name the frontend route in that file.
- Patch an architecture section only when a statement in it is now wrong. Leave file counts and the measured-on date alone.
- In the final message, name the doc you created or updated.

## Things Cursor must NOT do
- Do not finish a behavior change with the old description still in the doc.
- Do not add a second doc in `../passion/` for a feature already described under `docs/`.
- Do not put product behavior into `.cursor/rules/` or a skill. Those files tell the agent how to work.
- Do not refresh unrelated sections of the architecture docs.

## Real examples from the codebase
- Doorloom webhook + stay push + the settings card: `docs/DOORLOOM.md`.
- GRN approval posts stock: `docs/GRN_MODULE.md`.
- API facts by section: `PASSION_LARAVEL_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
